# Build context excludes.
#
# node_modules is not merely large here — it is a CORRECTNESS problem. The
# Dockerfile runs `COPY package*.json` -> `npm ci` -> `COPY . .`, so a
# node_modules present in the context is copied OVER the one npm ci just
# installed, replacing Linux packages with whatever the developer's machine
# (Windows, a different Node version, different optional deps) happens to
# hold. It has never bitten because the two machines that build this image
# have no node_modules on disk — that is luck, not design.

node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/

# Runtime/secret files. Vite reads .env at build time, but the deploy passes
# every VITE_* as a build ARG (see docker-compose.yml), and an ARG wins over a
# .env file. Excluding it removes the ambiguity entirely.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
